<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Attambelos VII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 2nd century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Attambelos VII was king of Characene, the trading kingdom at the head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>, in the early 2nd century CE. When the Roman emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a> advanced down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> to the Gulf in 116 CE, Attambelos received him and submitted. His kingdom, usually a Parthian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>, controlled the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charax-spasinou">Charax Spasinou</a> and its trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palmyra">Palmyra</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/attambelos-vii.jpg" alt="Attambelos VII" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NordNordWest · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Charakene.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
